OL,3,GNEWSACouncil calls for accountability
OL,4,Aover sea sewage
OL,5,
OL,6,FCouncillors have called for
OL,7,Faccountability over an incident which
OL,8,Fled sewage to be pumped into the sea.
OL,10,FAccidental damage to a main sewer pipe
OL,11,Fin Middlesbrough on 26 June led
OL,12,FNorthumbrian Water to carry out several
OL,13,F"heavily diluted" discharges to avoid
OL,14,Fthe local system backing up with
OL,15,Fsewage.
OL,17,F"No swim" alerts were later issued by
OL,18,FRedcar and Cleveland Council, affecting
OL,19,Fbeaches from Hartlepool to Saltburn -
OL,20,Fbut not until three days later, when it
OL,21,Fwas told about the incident.
OL,23,APub: 14-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NE Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,393,390,260,160,0,100
